  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_9a9796ac734544508684f3916aaccdff",
      "statement": "The workspace is a clean-sheet split: crates/logic owns all behavioral state and decisions as a pure decision core with no async, I/O, clocks, randomness, or locks, while crates/celld is only an effect executor and adapter host.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Cargo.toml#L1-L5",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:462368a26313f48ed93009e7cd4f07d3415bc44514868055ae8b0535a168acc8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/Cargo.toml#L4-L6",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:423b779a9a2f67032d8a8a506dd6566337fe1febea842ebc2696decf5743b80c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cbb3d34eb9fa4fc489517f43ec1d2bfd",
      "statement": "crates/celld is the executable that embeds V8, runs HTTP and peer listeners, owns SQLite files and the object-store client, and runs one serial actor which is the only caller of celld_logic::on_event.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L5-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cc3b6442ee100cdc295f066e59e0a497024a3d4e851a316478a0c0f4b1e90fdf:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L9-L13",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2f5ed6e16efd157fbeb245daba51a68897b5c4de78db5a905ca4024d0ec8ccbe:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_688d85fab03a4e18ab0a08df2e09f2ab",
      "statement": "A cell is a Durable Object: a named server with its own private SQLite database, and cells share no database.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L8-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f339ee6b4186d7e54274756d33eb922ed0e5faeeca27b6ea4450c9525425328:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3f3bae3bc5a44466b51eb5848e18176f",
      "statement": "The fleet bucket is the root of authority: it stores the deployments, the cell state, the ownership records, the node leases, and the peer-authentication secret.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L141-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5a9fc7138bf383286b411609965feb0b62254bfefbc4b8928a603b4c577d0dd7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3a0a1c8ac4c84e31b732728a7e48bc64",
      "statement": "A node claims a cell by a conditional bucket write, so the object store decides who wins and two nodes cannot both claim the same cell; the claim expires unless renewed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L19-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ed258f3e2c2163ce9d58218f19df2308c5a3392d25eed05aeaad47a1a9e91c6b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L38-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ae523cd073599474a536600bab0bcf137eff6e2da052991e1d1e3d3f59b617d3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_25840bfa3b5941e8904e23a594634859",
      "statement": "The ownership record names the owner node's session and carries a fencing epoch; every activation advances the epoch徒 and the replicator writes each cell's SQLite data under cells/<cell>/ltx/e<epoch>/, so an epoch never has two writers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L108-L131",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c319763a073c6d3abac29d8f72c4032a6bea862070bef7d441a2d51e3ac2d9d2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3dcadb2051f744208261df527953b5c1",
      "statement": "The object store must provide a conditional create, a conditional overwrite, and read-after-write consistency; qualified stores are Amazon S3, Cloudflare R2, Tigris, Google Cloud Storage, and Azure Blob Storage.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L16-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63b9f9cfab832c55c5983ed79994404f5dc5d0db229214de3f829128d46e7ceb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_129f6aff03444983baf2227d5306ad93",
      "statement": "crates/celld runs one serial actor that serializes every event through celld_logic::on_event and polls its mailbox, timers, and in-flight effect futures together, so monotonic lease ticks can fence the node even when a storage operation remains hung.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L7-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c2d0a985bbc0c2856fb26e6593936e0a884bfbdc3bf7e5c9aece6a58538bc1fc:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L9-L13",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2f5ed6e16efd157fbeb245daba51a68897b5c4de78db5a905ca4024d0ec8ccbe:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1bc3e2529afc4b74827299d9eedc7e28",
      "statement": "The core never reads a clock: it remembers what it was told through events, and node authority is evaluated at ask time against the published lease expiry on the monotonic clock rather than by trusting a timer to have fired.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L591-L599",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e5d7d3d25f1ce8f8d0e3ee2b34d280942aedc06ef2a64aac97ae8082ea4183e8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L714-L737",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6085ed359ef13e7c64247f04dc411bad80b8d85a8dee6fe0eaa9b9e982fbee5b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6f401faec3d04987bf250291850b8b0c",
      "statement": "celld-logic has no I/O so that the clock, the randomness, and the object store are interfaces and a deterministic simulator can drive the core, injecting latency, compare-and-swap races, and lost responses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/Cargo.toml#L4-L6",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:423b779a9a2f67032d8a8a506dd6566337fe1febea842ebc2696decf5743b80c:"
